From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Subject: doc: do not treat doxygen warnings as errors

Upstream turned doxygen warnings into errors (commit 32165009), but the
doc tree was written against an older doxygen: current releases report
hundreds of warnings (unknown commands from alias-in-formula usage such
as \src inside \f$... \f$, unexpanded aliases, unresolved @ref targets,
mismatched \return documentation). Failing the whole package build on
doc cosmetics is wrong, so build the documentation with warnings
tolerated, as before.

--- a/doc/Doxyfile.in
+++ b/doc/Doxyfile.in
@@ -751,7 +751,7 @@
 # a warning is encountered.
 # The default value is: NO.

-WARN_AS_ERROR          = YES
+WARN_AS_ERROR          = NO

 # This WARN_NO_PARAMDOC option can be enabled to get warnings for functions that
 # are documented, but have no documentation for their parameters or return
